# Files permitted to contain credential-SHAPED text.
#
# Read only by `python main.py --preflight scan --committed`, which is the
# question that matters before a push: could a secret reach a commit? The
# whole-tree scan ignores this file entirely and still reports everything.
#
# Every entry here is an exemption someone has to justify. The rule of thumb:
# exempt a file only if it cannot pass without a string the scanner would flag
# -- and say so in a comment.
#
# This file lists PATHS, never values. Do not put a secret here: the allowlist
# cannot store one safely and would itself be committed.

# --- redaction / egress test fixtures ---------------------------------------
